{#- Guidance Layer -#}
## Task
Build an entity registry from project initialization materials. You are only responsible for identifying entities and their possible aliases; do not make chapter-level factual judgments.

Output Controls:
- Prioritize characters, core locations, key items, organizations, and core concepts; do not list ordinary scene props.
- Keep `notes` as empty strings or brief sentences under 20 characters; do not expand with background explanations.
- `entity_id` must be stable and concise; do not output duplicates of the same entity.
- This artifact serves as the canonical entity registry for subsequent source artifacts; characters, locations, items, organizations, and concepts must receive unique `entity_id` here.
- Old names, misnames, past lives, nicknames, and internal organization titles may only go into the same entity's `aliases`; do not create separate synonymous entities.
- If an alias does not explicitly appear in the input materials, do not invent it; uncertain designations should be written as brief risk hints in `notes`, not registered as formal aliases.
- Subsequent chapter prompts will only reference `entity_id` or projections from this registry; therefore `name` must be the authoritative display name; do not mix in stage states or plot explanations.

## Field Content Constraints
- Each entity object may only contain `entity_id`, `name`, `entity_type`, `aliases`, `source`, `notes`.
- `entity_type` may only be `character`, `location`, `item`, `organization`, `concept`, `unknown`.
- Field names must use only the English `snake_case` keys listed above; categories, backgrounds, or relationship or chapter factual explanations should be merged into `notes`.

